        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(message): ignore populated location on text sends",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes a Telegram delivery failure where model-generated `message(action=\"send\")` calls could populate the optional `location` object during an ordinary text or media reply. The shared outbound runner correctly rejected the mixed payload with:\n\n```text\nLocation sends cannot be combined with message text or media.\n```\n\nThat dropped an otherwise complete user-visible reply.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nTelegram exposed `location` on the broad `send` action, so tool-call generators could fill it even when the intended send mode was text or media. The original patch repaired this in the shared runner by silently deleting location, but that weakened the public mixed-payload contract across every channel and could discard an intentional location request.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis redesign preserves the shared invariant and fixes the producer boundary instead:\n\n- adds an explicit Telegram `send-location` action for intentional native pins and venues;\n- keeps legacy location-only `send` calls compatible;\n- marks agent message-tool calls with an internal origin and removes incidental Telegram location only from model-authored text/media sends;\n- performs private host-owned Telegram normalization after the requested action is authorized, then translates `send-location` to canonical `send` for existing durable/gateway delivery;\n- preserves strict rejection for direct/API callers that intentionally mix location with text, media, presentation, or interactive content;\n- keeps `asVideoNote` on its existing cross-channel schema scope and limits the location schema to the current Telegram channel.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNormal Telegram text and media replies—including URL/path, attachment, image, and base64 `buffer` media forms—are delivered when a model fills an unrelated location field. Explicit location sends remain standalone and validated. Existing direct callers still receive an actionable error for invalid mixed payloads rather than losing location data silently.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Exact-head real Telegram delivery proof\n\nA temporary, uncommitted runner loaded the real Telegram action adapter/runtime from exact head `ec137200b4075780c6438897323ed519217a679e`, resolved the configured bot credential privately, and delivered through the real Telegram Bot API to a live chat. The token, account, and chat target are redacted from the published transcript; the runner was removed and the worktree remained clean.\n\n- Redacted live transcript: https://gist.github.com/snotty/d3ca4e6b5d473b8513570bb7dab007ea\n- Raw transcript: https://gist.githubusercontent.com/snotty/d3ca4e6b5d473b8513570bb7dab007ea/raw/pr111404-live-telegram-proof.txt\n- SHA-256: `b3964ca63671c39d6c23d00b6c5120288fe5ee4d70c25ed2139c4298f56465ce`\n\nThe exact-head run produced three visible Telegram messages in sequence:\n\n```text\nsendMessage -> messageId 8707: incidental-location text delivered, location removed\nsendPhoto   -> messageId 8708: incidental-location image delivered, location removed\nsendLocation -> messageId 8709: explicit standalone location delivered, location preserved\ndirect mixed content+location -> rejected before delivery with the documented error\n```\n\nThis is a real final-head Bot API delivery, not a mocked or placeholder-token Vitest harness. The direct mixed-payload check used the same exact-head adapter/runtime but intentionally produced no Telegram message because rejection before delivery is the required behavior.\n\nMantis native Desktop automation was also requested with the exact maintainer-suggested command. The workflow accepted the syntax but its authorization gate declined the contributor account because native Mantis runs require repository write/maintain/admin permission. The live-bot proof above is therefore the contributor-accessible evidence path requested by ClawSweeper.\n\nEarlier Mantis native Telegram Desktop evidence remains useful for the original user-visible failure and earlier candidate behavior:\n\n- Run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29691948840\n- Artifact: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29691948840/artifacts/8444147473\n\n### Telegram-only seam refinement\n\nThe latest head removes `normalizeMessageActionRequest` from the public `ChannelMessageActionAdapter` / Plugin SDK contract. The repair now lives in a private host-owned Telegram normalizer used by both local `runMessageAction` and Gateway `message.action` after requested-action authorization. Non-Telegram channels are explicit no-ops; direct callers remain strict.\n\n### Validation\n\nThe branch was refreshed with current `main` (`c715d89de8`) and the core-test boundary regression caught by CI was fixed by replacing the Gateway test's bundled Telegram runtime import with a core-local adapter fixture. Exact-head local validation:\n\n```text\nFocused Vitest: 11 files / 593 tests passed\nCore tsgo extension boundary: passed\nPlugin SDK API baseline: passed\nProduction TypeScript (tsgo:prod): passed\nTest TypeScript (check:test-types): passed\noxfmt check: passed\noxlint: 0 warnings, 0 errors\ngit diff --check: passed\n```\n\nRegression coverage verifies:\n\n- explicit `send-location` is authorized before translation;\n- a `send`-only allowlist cannot authorize `send-location`;\n- explicit location translates through the common runner to canonical durable `send`;\n- direct callers retain mixed-payload rejection;\n- incidental location repair is limited to model-authored Telegram sends;\n- text, image, attachment, URL/path, and base64 `buffer` media are recognized before hydration;\n- top-level `image` reaches durable Telegram media handling;\n- `asVideoNote` retains all-configured schema visibility while location remains current-channel scoped;\n- the private Telegram normalizer is shared by local and Gateway paths and no public Plugin SDK rewrite hook remains.\n\nThe repository `check:changed` wrapper could not launch locally because the installed Crabbox binary failed its own `--version`/`--help` sanity check; focused tests, boundary checks, production/test type checks, formatter, linter, Plugin SDK baseline, and diff validation completed locally. Hosted CI is the authoritative full-suite run.\n\n\n",
